feat(orders): add bulk 'serve all' action for ready orders

When all items in an order are in 'ready' status, a 'Tout servir'
(Mark all as served) button appears in the expanded order detail.
This lets the chef advance all items to 'served' in one click instead
of validating each item individually through the pending → preparing →
ready → served flow.

The backend already supports bulk validation: POST to
/cash/kds/{station}/orders/{id}/validate without item_index advances
all items to the next status. This PR wires up that capability in
the mobile PWA frontend.

Changes:
- src/views/orders/OrdersList.vue: added allItemsReady() helper,
  markAllServed() async function, and 'Tout servir' button in the
  expanded order detail section
- src/i18n/locales/fr/orders.json: added orders.actions.serveAll
- src/i18n/locales/en/orders.json: added orders.actions.serveAll
- src/i18n/locales/es/orders.json: added orders.actions.serveAll
- tests/unit/OrdersList.test.mjs: 3 new tests for the bulk action
  (button visible when all ready, hidden when items pending, API call
  fires with empty body)